## Verify the artifacts

Verify each chart and each image by its digest before you install the chart by its digest. The README of each chart gives the commands: {{range $i, $c := .Charts}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}[{{$c.Name}}](https://github.com/{{$.GitHubRepo}}/blob/{{$.Commit}}/charts/{{$c.Name}}/README.md#verify-a-release){{end}}.

The SBOM of each image lists the Go modules of the service binary. It does not list the npm packages of the web UIs, which are in the binary.

## cdrlab

The release has a `cdrlab` archive for `linux-amd64`, `linux-arm64`, `darwin-amd64` and `darwin-arm64`. `cdrlab up` starts the compose lab of this release in the current directory, with only Docker and Compose on the host. Download the archive of your platform, verify the signature of the checksum file, the checksum and the provenance of the archive, then start the lab:

```sh
platform=linux-amd64
gh release download {{.ImageTag}} --repo {{.GitHubRepo}} \
  --pattern "cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-$platform.tar.gz" --pattern "cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-checksums.txt*"
cosign verify-blob cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-checksums.txt --bundle cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-checksums.txt.sigstore.json \
  --certificate-identity https://github.com/{{.GitHubRepo}}/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com
sha256sum --check --ignore-missing cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-checksums.txt  # macOS: shasum -a 256 --check --ignore-missing
gh attestation verify "cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-$platform.tar.gz" --repo {{.GitHubRepo}} \
  --signer-workflow {{.GitHubRepo}}/.github/workflows/release.yml --source-ref refs/heads/main
tar -xzf "cdrlab-{{.ImageTag}}-$platform.tar.gz" cdrlab
./cdrlab up
```

With Go, `go install github.com/lukemundy/cdr-lab/cli/cdrlab/cmd/cdrlab@{{.Version}}` builds the same `cdrlab` from the source, with no cosign signature.
